# Only needed for `cre workflow simulate --broadcast`, which submits the
# verdict write through the Arc Testnet MockKeystoneForwarder for real.
# A plain (non-broadcast) simulate needs neither this file nor a funded key —
# the CLI falls back to a built-in sentinel key and warns; `--broadcast`
# rejects that sentinel explicitly.
#
# Nobody issues this key. Generate a throwaway EVM account yourself:
#
#     cast wallet new          # Foundry, already a repo dependency
#
# and fund its address with Arc Testnet gas at https://faucet.circle.com
# (gas on Arc is USDC, so the same faucet covers gas and any test payment).
#
# 64 hex characters. A `0x` prefix is accepted and stripped; wrapping quotes
# are not. Use a fresh burner — never a key that holds anything on mainnet.
#
# This is a CLI/tooling key, not Verdikt's verifier identity: the workflow
# holds no key and signs nothing itself (docs/spikes/cre.md, CRE-2).
CRE_ETH_PRIVATE_KEY=
